## Key Architecture Points

### Agent Selection Algorithm
1. Check specific agent type requested in task
2. Evaluate agent availability via `is_available()`
3. Calculate confidence scores for tool patterns
4. Select agent with highest average confidence

### Tool Integration Strategy
- Map to existing commands in [src-tauri/src/commands/](mdc:src-tauri/src/commands/)
- Use pattern matching on tool names: `tool_call.name.contains(pattern)`
- Maintain backward compatibility with single-agent workflows

### Error Handling Pattern
```rust
// Use appropriate AgentError variants
AgentError::Other(format!("Browser agent error: {}", details))
AgentError::ToolError("Specific tool error".to_string())
```

## Development Requirements

### Must-Do After Each Change
```bash
# ALWAYS run this after modifying Rust code
~/.cargo/bin/cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml
```

### Registration Process
1. Implement `BrowserAgent` with `SpecializedAgent` trait
2. Add `browser_agent` module to [src-tauri/src/agents/mod.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agents/mod.rs)
3. Uncomment and implement in `AgentFactory::initialize_default_agents()`
4. Test compilation and basic functionality

